The legal text is the Constitution of the Republic of The Gambia, 1997 ("reprinted 2002"), as published by the National Assembly of
The Gambia (https://assembly.gm/constitution; the same text is on the Ministry of Justice site, https://www.moj.gm), retrieved
30 October 2026. The site states no licence and no restriction on reuse. The text of a constitution is an official legislative
text; we have not verified whether the Copyright Act 2004 expressly excludes such texts.

Changes made by Lexifina: the text was converted to one Markdown file per section, line breaks within a paragraph were joined,
marginal notes and page numbers were dropped, and typographic quotes and dashes were normalised. The wording of the law was not
changed. The National Assembly does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages and the tools) are dedicated to the
public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
